  "notes": [
    "Positions only: every byte comes from the user's own ROM at extraction time.",
    "Only decoded resources are listed. Data whose format is still unknown (the game data at 0x100000) stays in the ROM images the build reads; it is added here as each format is worked out.",
    "Sprites: every frame of sprite_frame_records (program ROM 0x130000) as an indexed PNG, 4 or 8 bits a pixel, with the palette sprite_palettes.json says it is drawn with (positions in the program ROM, tools/palette_census.py); pen 0 is transparent. frames.json says where each goes back in the sprite ROM.",
    "Tile sheets are 8-bit indexed PNGs in color: the 16 palettes the sheet's tiles are shown with the most (tile_palettes.json, positions in the program ROM), a tile's pixels at its palette's slot * 16 + pen, so index & 15 is the pen; pen 0 is transparent. Each sheet's JSON says every tile's palette.",
    "PCM rate is nominal (half the RF5C68 output rate): the real pitch is set per sample by the Z80 driver."
  ],
